@page "/"

<PageTitle>HeadlessUI.Blazor</PageTitle>

<div class="demo-page">
    <header class="demo-header">
        <h1>HeadlessUI.Blazor</h1>
        <p>A headless component library for Blazor — zero styles, full accessibility, complete control.</p>
    </header>

    <section class="demo-section">
        <h2>What is this?</h2>
        <p>
            HeadlessUI.Blazor provides accessible, behaviour-complete component primitives with no visual
            opinion at all. The library ships zero CSS — you own every pixel.
        </p>
        <p style="margin-top:.75rem">
            Each component handles WAI-ARIA wiring, keyboard navigation, focus management, and
            data-attribute hooks (<code>data-state</code>, <code>data-disabled</code>) so you can style with
            pure CSS selectors.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="demo-section">
        <h2>Browse components</h2>
        <p>Pick a component from the sidebar to see live demos and the source code that produced them.</p>

        <ul class="component-list">
            <li><a href="button">Button</a> — polymorphic, loading/disabled state, render-prop context.</li>
            <li><a href="switch">Switch</a> — accessible on/off toggle with full keyboard support.</li>
            <li><a href="checkbox">Checkbox</a> — tri-state checkbox with form integration.</li>
            <li><a href="radiogroup">Radio Group</a> — single-select group with roving tabindex.</li>
            <li><a href="listbox">Listbox</a> — custom select with single/multi mode and typeahead.</li>
            <li><a href="combobox">Combobox</a> — typeable autocomplete with consumer-driven filtering.</li>
            <li><a href="menu">Menu</a> — accessible dropdown with keyboard nav and typeahead.</li>
            <li><a href="popover">Popover</a> — non-modal floating panel with focus management and group coordination.</li>
            <li><a href="transition">Transition</a> — CSS class-based enter/leave animations.</li>
            <li><a href="field">Field / Input</a> — form primitives with auto-wired ARIA labels and descriptions.</li>
            <li><a href="fieldset">Fieldset</a> — group form controls together with a legend, with cascading disabled state.</li>
            <li><a href="dialog">Dialog</a> — accessible modal with focus trap, scroll lock, and inert background.</li>
            <li><a href="tabs">Tabs</a> — accessible tab group with roving tabindex and keyboard nav.</li>
            <li><a href="disclosure">Disclosure</a> — single show/hide region with full ARIA wiring.</li>
            <li><a href="accordion">Accordion</a> — multi-panel collapsible group, single or multiple.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>
</div>
